== Notes ==
* The Visage's deactivated mask can be still targeted by effects such as {{i|Anima Sola}}.

== Trivia ==
* The Visage started as a boss versus screen mockup by ''Antibirth'' artist '''NotYourSagittarius''' in January 2015, alongside {{e|Reap Creep}} and a scrapped posthumous version of {{e|Dingle}} known as "The Mass".
* The Visage appears to be a fiery variation of the {{e|Mask of Infamy}}.
** In a way, it can be seen as the posthumous version of the Mask of Infamy.
* The Visage in ''Antibirth'' bore a grey and purple color palette better suited for the {{s|Mausoleum}}, while the Visage in ''Repentance'' has been recolored black and red to match the {{s|Gehenna}} floor.
** Prior to patch [[V1.7.5]], many of its attacks were still purple.
* The back of the mask shows many small children being burned while the mask is alive.
** This is probably a reference to the fact that in Gehenna, some kings of Judah sacrificed their children by fire.
** In ''Antibirth'', instead of many children, there was a singular Isaac head in the back of the mask.
** This is a reference to the original Mask of Infamy from the ''Wrath Of The Lamb'' DLC of the original flash game, as it had a small head peeking through the crack behind the boss.

== Bugs ==
{{Bug|Using the console to spawn the mask by itself (id 903.1) will crash the game. All other parts of the Visage can be spawned safely.}}
{{Bug|If a slash from {{i|Dark Arts}} / {{p|Soul of Judas}} reduces the mask's hp to 0, it will die and despawn instead of deactivating, leaving only the heart to be fought.}}
{{bug|If The Visage's mask is chained by {{i|Anima Sola}} down when it runs out of HP, it will outright die instead of becoming temporarily inactive, leaving only the heart to be fought.}}
{{bug|If The Visage's mask is defeated by knockback damage from {{I|Hemoptysis}} or {{I|Knockout Drops}}, it will outright die instead of becoming temporarily inactive.}}

